  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Organisation Summary: Youth Projects Development Platform (YPDP), is a registered National Youth-Led Non- Governmental Organizationbased in Lusaka. The Organization was established in 2017 and obtained its legal status on 3rd August 2021. The aim of theorganization is to create a more developed Zambia and champion the economic independence of young people. YPDP focuses on Economic Development, Education, Innovation and Inventions, environmental protection, conservation and Climate Change.

Vision: YPDP envision a Zambia in which youths are educated, their ideas, entrepreneurial initiatives, inventions and innovations become a reality and an environment that is healthy and sustainable.

Mission: YPDP&#x2019;s mission is to empower youths in creating a moredeveloped Zambia and champion the economic independence of young people by educating the vulnerable, promoting and supporting cooperative entrepreneurial initiatives, inventions and innovations as well as a health and sustained environment.

Core Values
&#x2022; Love: Our actions are inspired by love towards humanity and other living and non-living creation.
&#x2022; Nature
&#x2022; Transparency
&#x2022; Accountability
&#x2022; Partnership
&#x2022; Human Development
&#x2022; Commitment to Positive Change

Our Main Objectives
1. To promote youth invention and innovations through mobilization of resources, partnership and enhancement of kills
2. To promote, encourage and sustain the establishment of youth cooperatives and entrepreneurial initiatives through the implementation of 100 Youths
3. To support vulnerable children and young people by awarding them partial or full sponsorships
4. To promote a health and sustainable natural environment through the implementation of the Green-Clean Youth Response</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Projects Development Platform</narrative>
